  "name": "development rung, both pad branches (T32 / d96 / f256, 12 heads of 8 over 4 KV heads)",
  "norm_top_limb_is_full_byte": false,
  "note": "LANE STAGE 30: rung-K4's PADDED layout exactly \u2014 t_pad 32, d_pad 128, h_pad 16, f_pad 256, the same nine domain logs and helper counts, the same 9-row generalised endpoint \u2014 with two true sizes moved onto their pads: 32 tokens instead of 24 and hidden 256 instead of 192. So Dom::T (2^5), Dom::Kv (32*4*8 = 2^10) and Dom::F (32*256 = 2^13) DO NOT PAD while Ht, L, D, Q, S and Tab still do \u2014 which is 125M's own padded-domain set at a size the Rust test filter runs in seconds. Ruling P-1's pad-zero term is therefore absent from host slots 02 (SC_TZC), 16 (SC_KVZC) and 18 (SC_FZC), and the last two lose the support indicator and one degree with it: 4,742,728 B against rung-K4's 4,743,128, the 400-byte difference being (10 + 1) + (13 + 1) = 25 published round values of 16 B",
